[2026-03-14T22:22:17.881Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GQ49ZR8EE4VphCkdkj9LZg","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Reference Guide\n\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Here's what you need to know:\n\n## Quick Setup\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun, then authenticate by setting your `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable from https://app.replay.io settings.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n**Recording & Uploading:**\n- `replayio record [url]` – Launch Replay Browser and capture a session\n- `replayio upload [ids...]` – Upload recordings to your account\n- `replayio list` – View all local recordings with status\n\n**Account Management:**\n- `replayio login` – Authenticate via browser\n- `replayio logout` – Sign out (doesn't invalidate API keys)\n\n**Maintenance:**\n- `replayio remove [ids...]` – Delete recordings locally\n- `replayio update` – Update the Replay Browser\n- `replayio upload-source-maps` – Upload source maps with options for grouping and filtering\n\n## Typical Workflow\n\nStart recording with `replayio record https://myapp.com`, then use `replayio upload <id>` to share the recording. You can integrate the Replay MCP Server into Claude for enhanced debugging by configuring it with your API key.\n\nPass `-h` or `--help` to any command for additional options."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ab1d8c1-1a0a-4757-b233-42915719b9b9","uuid":"260ec232-843a-4d0a-ba25-ff880b858c54","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Reference Guide\n\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Here's what you need to know:\n\n## Quick Setup\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun, then authenticate by setting your `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable from https://app.replay.io settings.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n**Recording & Uploading:**\n- `replayio record [url]` – Launch Replay Browser and capture a session\n- `replayio upload [ids...]` – Upload recordings to your account\n- `replayio list` – View all local recordings with status\n\n**Account Management:**\n- `replayio login` – Authenticate via browser\n- `replayio logout` – Sign out (doesn't invalidate API keys)\n\n**Maintenance:**\n- `replayio remove [ids...]` – Delete recordings locally\n- `replayio update` – Update the Replay Browser\n- `replayio upload-source-maps` – Upload source maps with options for grouping and filtering\n\n## Typical Workflow\n\nStart recording with `replayio record https://myapp.com`, then use `replayio upload <id>` to share the recording. You can integrate the Replay MCP Server into Claude for enhanced debugging by configuring it with your API key.\n\nPass `-h` or `--help` to any command for additional options.","durationMs":3249,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
