[2026-03-14T22:22:19.970Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PzjdQ5TeMyi9Ewskex2xqk","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Documentation - Complete Content\n\n**name:** replay-mcp\n\n**description:** \"Use Replay MCP to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\"\n\n**allowed-tools:** Bash(replayio:*), mcp__replay\n\n## Overview\n\nReplay MCP enables investigation of https://replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data. The tool functions like \"a time machine,\" allowing examination of app behavior at any point.\n\nKey principle: avoid premature conclusions. Instead, follow this methodology:\n\n1. Frame the investigation as a specific question\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Form hypotheses supported by gathered evidence\n5. Present conclusions with supporting data\n\n## Essential Concepts\n\n**Point:** A discrete execution moment when a JavaScript statement runs or a significant state-affecting event occurs.\n\n**Element:** A persistent DOM element reference independent of specific points, existing throughout its lifetime in the recording.\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what occurred and when:\n- Errors (UncaughtException, ReactException)\n- Timeline (ConsoleMessages, LocalStorage, NetworkRequest, ReactRenders)\n- Sources (ListSources, ReadSource, SearchSources)\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify causation:\n- Dependencies (GetStack, ControlDependency)\n- Details (DescribePoint, InspectElement, ReactComponents, Logpoint, Evaluate)\n\n## Recommended Approaches\n\nIdentify relevant code, verify execution, and examine execution details. The Logpoint tool proves particularly valuable for tracking expression values across multiple executions. For timing issues, locate associated points and use ControlDependency to explore prerequisite events and delays."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ab1d8c1-1a0a-4757-b233-42915719b9b9","uuid":"471e002a-4d7f-4fda-b9c0-35fef6861be6","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Documentation - Complete Content\n\n**name:** replay-mcp\n\n**description:** \"Use Replay MCP to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\"\n\n**allowed-tools:** Bash(replayio:*), mcp__replay\n\n## Overview\n\nReplay MCP enables investigation of https://replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data. The tool functions like \"a time machine,\" allowing examination of app behavior at any point.\n\nKey principle: avoid premature conclusions. Instead, follow this methodology:\n\n1. Frame the investigation as a specific question\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Form hypotheses supported by gathered evidence\n5. Present conclusions with supporting data\n\n## Essential Concepts\n\n**Point:** A discrete execution moment when a JavaScript statement runs or a significant state-affecting event occurs.\n\n**Element:** A persistent DOM element reference independent of specific points, existing throughout its lifetime in the recording.\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what occurred and when:\n- Errors (UncaughtException, ReactException)\n- Timeline (ConsoleMessages, LocalStorage, NetworkRequest, ReactRenders)\n- Sources (ListSources, ReadSource, SearchSources)\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify causation:\n- Dependencies (GetStack, ControlDependency)\n- Details (DescribePoint, InspectElement, ReactComponents, Logpoint, Evaluate)\n\n## Recommended Approaches\n\nIdentify relevant code, verify execution, and examine execution details. The Logpoint tool proves particularly valuable for tracking expression values across multiple executions. For timing issues, locate associated points and use ControlDependency to explore prerequisite events and delays.","durationMs":4777,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
